{
  "case_id": "2018-18-726",
  "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Was -- was this an excessive political consideration?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, if that's right, then your defense is not really that we can't tell the difference between excessive and non-excessive because, under any measure, this is excessive, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, why -- why should we assume, Mr. Sullivan, that everything would stay the same?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What would be an example of a situation where a -- the drawing of a district would be impermissible, would constitute impermissible political gerrymandering in your opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, is it your -- is it your position that this -- what -- what was done in Maryland would be okay under any test, but you're not going to tell us which of the possible tests is the right test, or are you just saying the wrong test was done, was used here, so we should send it back to -- for the Court to find some other test which you're not going to identify and then apply that to the facts of your case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael B. Kimberly (Appellees)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY ON BEHALF OF THE APPELLEES\nMR. KIMBERLY: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nI'd like to begin with just a very succinct statement of what our claim is and what our theory is.\nWhen state officials use redistricting to burden a particular group of voters because of their political views, with the express goal of making it harder for those -- for that group of voters to win elections, and when that goal is achieved so that group of voters is ordinarily doomed to usual electoral defeat under the map, and when the state cannot come forward with a legitimate governmental interest to justify the burdens imposed, the map has to be neutrally redrawn."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: What do we do about the referendum? The whole of the people had a chance to speak. Now I -- I understand that there are questions about how good a referendum that was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So you think if you have the redistricting controlled by one political party and it comes out that the districts reflect a significant benefit for that particular party, that's not enough to infer an intent to draw the districts with an eye to the partisan effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why not? You have intent, which on this case they -- all the leaders said, yeah, that's what we want to do, reduce the Republican representation by one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Steven M. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, there's a number of things wrong with that. The -- into the future is not proven at all. The map that was developed, the expert testimony agreed that it was a competitive map. Independent sources said it was a plus two Democratic."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Steven M. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the reason that this test doesn't work, as counsel revealed, is that it abandons what this Court or members of this Court, including Justice Kagan in her Gill concurrence, have identified as an essential evil of gerrymandering, which is the politicians getting one over on the people and not letting the people's will control what the map is going to be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-726",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7c93090250b4c2bb8d0a8a29e105e39bf883613f07bba4b1c54c1aa7792aefbd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7c93090250b4-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
